### 1. Review of `R1`–`R10` ([`DRAFT2.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/_review/DRAFT2.md))

- **R1. AGREE.** `Q7.10` ([`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L258)) and `F6` ([`R4_RATIONALE.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/archive/decisions-2026-11-05/R4_RATIONALE.md#L292-L343)) omit `SIGPIPE`, inherited fds `>= 3`, `umask`, signal masks, loader injection, stack-page probing, `W^X`, and entry FP state. **Best long-term design, except one shortcut:** entry FP state alone does not give deterministic floats at slice 26; `C2` ([`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L40)) must also forbid implicit FMA contraction and canonicalize quiet-NaN payloads across LLVM and LCB.
- **R2. AGREE.** `TYPE-22@1` ([`types.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/types.md#L1498-L1515)) inlines constants at each use with no storage, and [`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L227) places `const` at slice 17 while slice 15/16 workloads need lookup tables. **Best long-term design, with one refinement:** give aggregate constants a read-only static `BlockId` in `C4` ([`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L58-L65)) so `borrow C as v` reuses `Q4.7` views (`StaticStr` already uses static roots in [`R4_RATIONALE.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/archive/decisions-2026-11-05/R4_RATIONALE.md#L225)).
- **R3. AGREE.** [`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L328) leaves wide arithmetic unplaced and slice 2 ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L212)) lacks bit/carry ops. **Shortcut in stated design:** splitting carry/wide-multiply into two separate scalar calls works around structs arriving at slice 9, duplicating work and losing single-instruction `adc`/`sbb`/`umulh` lowering. **Best long-term:** lower to single multi-result BIR ops (like `binOvf`, [`Concrete/README.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/Concrete/README.md#L99)) and expose two-field `Copy` structs at slice 9.
- **R4. AGREE.** Whole-root freezing (`OD15(a)`, `Q3.2`–`Q3.4` in [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L168-L185), `C5` in [`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L78)) prevents two disjoint mutable views of one array and overlap-safe intra-slice copies needed at slices 15 and 21–22. **Best long-term design:** make `split` a scoped `borrow mut` form matching `Q4.7` ([`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L237)) under the single root freeze, plus `copy_from`, `copy_within`, and `fill` with range-update laws.
- **R5. AGREE.** Decided wiping ([`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L846-L864)) and `C7` ([`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L98-L107)) leave move-source slots, register spills, callee frames, and core dumps unscoped, violating Rule 12 ([`PHILOSOPHY.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L116)). **Best long-term design:** specify move-source zeroing in `C4`/`C7`, prove callee-frame/spill scrubbing on LCB (named premise on LLVM) in `C10`/`R-0596`, and disable core dumps in the launcher when secret facts exist.
- **R6. AGREE.** Proof-order item 4 ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L107)) and `R-0495`/`R-0482` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L534-L537)) defer functional models to Phase E, while slices 7, 8, 15, and 18 require `#[proof(path)]` user theorems ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L217-L228)). **Best long-term design:** emit pure functional models with proved Core refinement from slice 8 (extending at 13/18/19) instead of writing throwaway fuel-indexed Core proofs first.
- **R7. AGREE.** `OD62` ([`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L1352)) covers unused locals and `OD18` ([`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L1308)) unreachable arms, leaving unused imports and dead private items uncovered in [`modules.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/modules.md). **Best long-term design:** unconditional compile error (Rules 2, 5, 15); Codex's "fact + policy first" is a two-mode shortcut. Note: unreachable private functions start at **slice 5**, unused imports/`pub` at **slice 17**.
- **R8. AGREE.** `R-0603` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L415)) puts `spec_version` in compiler outputs and `R-0589` ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L466)) versions `[policy]`/`[assumptions]` in `Concrete.toml`, but the package's target `spec_version` is missing. **Shortcut in stated placement:** deferring to Phase G is wrong because `Concrete.toml` already exists at slices 0–1 ([`ROADMAP.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/ROADMAP.md#L209-L210)). **Best long-term:** require `spec_version` in `Concrete.toml` at **slice 1 (`B1`)** with `R-0589`.
- **R9. AGREE.** `FFI-5` ([`ffi.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#L204-L235)) and `R-0286` ([`task_disposition.tsv`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/archive/roadmap-2026-11/task_disposition.tsv#L287)) omit incoming ABI, `with(...)`/grant rules, and entry premises for `#[export_name]`. **Best long-term design, with one required link:** [`decisions.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/decisions.md#L603) (`Q2/Q9`) already decides *"an exported function's precondition joins its foreign contract"*, so `#[requires]` on an export must also record a foreign-caller assumption in `[assumptions]` (`R-0589`) and `C10`.
- **R10. AGREE.** `FFI-7` ([`ffi.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#L272)) lacks `offset_of`, and `Q6.2` ([`R4_RATIONALE.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/archive/decisions-2026-11-05/R4_RATIONALE.md#L477-L494)) excludes `sizeof`/`alignof` from statically-known expressions. **Best long-term design, with one refinement:** because `C3` ([`FOUNDATION.md`](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/feature-gaps/agy/docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#L48)) fixes deterministic native struct layout in the target profile (`R-0502`), `offset_of(T, field)` is well-defined for all structs from **slice 9** (not only `#[repr(C)]`), tagged target-profile-dependent in `Q6.2`.

